# GTP Telemetry Analyzer — Project Architecture

## Overview

This repo contains two projects:

1. **gtp-telemetry/** — A React web app that parses iRacing `.ibt` telemetry files in the browser and runs a 14-step engineering analysis checklist. No backend; all parsing and analysis happens client-side.
2. **iracing-gtp-engineer-plugin/** — A Claude skill/plugin for iRacing GTP setup engineering (commands, references, IBT parsing via Python).

## Tech Stack (gtp-telemetry)

| Layer | Technology | Version |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| Language | TypeScript | ~5.9 |
| Framework | React | 19 |
| Build | Vite | 7 |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS | 4 (via `@tailwindcss/vite`) |
| State | Zustand | 5 |
| Charts | Recharts | 3 |
| PDF Export | jsPDF + html2canvas | |
| YAML | js-yaml | 4 |
| Lint | ESLint 9 (flat config) | |

## Directory Layout

```
gtp-telemetry/
  src/
    lib/           # Core logic: IBT parser, analysis engine, car/track profiles, types, constants
    components/
      upload/      # DropZone for file upload
      dashboard/   # 14+ analysis panels (one per checklist item)
      shared/      # Reusable UI primitives: Card, TabBar, StatusBadge, MetricRow
    store/         # Zustand store (session-store.ts)
    data/
      car-quirks/  # Per-car JSON configuration files
      tracks/      # Per-track JSON profiles
```

## Key Conventions

### Imports and Paths
- Use the `@/` path alias (maps to `src/`) for all imports.
- Use named exports for components and utilities. Lazy-loaded dashboard panels use dynamic `import()` with `.then()` destructuring.

### TypeScript
- Strict mode enabled. All types defined in `src/lib/types.ts`.
- Use `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/aliases.
- Use `as const` assertions for constant objects and arrays.
- Prefer `Record<K, V>` over index signatures.

### React Components
- Functional components only, no classes.
- Props defined as inline interfaces within the component file (not exported separately unless shared).
- Components are named exports matching the file name.
- Dashboard panels receive the full `SessionAnalysis` object as an `analysis` prop.

### State Management
- Single Zustand store in `src/store/session-store.ts`.
- Store handles the full file → parse → analyze pipeline.
- No context providers; components access state via `useSessionStore()`.

### Styling
- Tailwind CSS 4 utility classes exclusively. No CSS modules, no styled-components.
- Dark motorsport theme using CSS custom properties (`var(--color-*)`) defined in `src/index.css`.
- Color constants in `src/lib/constants.ts` (COLORS object) for Recharts and programmatic use.
- Cards use `bg-[var(--color-card)]` with `border-[var(--color-card-border)]` and `rounded-xl`.

### Build & Dev
- `npm run dev` — Start Vite dev server
- `npm run build` — `tsc -b && vite build`
- `npm run lint` — ESLint
- No test framework is configured yet.

### Code Splitting
- Dashboard panels are lazy-loaded via `React.lazy()`.
- Vite manual chunks split recharts, jspdf, html2canvas, and react-vendor bundles.

## Domain Context

This app is for **iRacing GTP Hypercar telemetry analysis**. The root `SKILL.md` contains comprehensive domain knowledge about:
- The five GTP cars (BMW, Cadillac, Porsche, Acura, Ferrari)
- IBT binary file format and parsing
- Telemetry channel names and units
- Setup parameter engineering (suspension, aero, tyres, diff, brakes)
- Analysis workflow and thresholds

Reference `SKILL.md` for any iRacing domain questions.
